    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer multilayer infrared filter on CaF2 (Daimon-20) substrate with air incidence at normal angle. Stack sequence: zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2/zns/mgf2 (22 layers total, alternating). Initialize layer thicknesses using physics-aware bootstrap: calculate quarter-wave thickness t = λ_center/(4×n) for Bragg mirror layers using λ_center = 4400 nm and estimated effective indices (zns n≈2.3, mgf2 n≈1.35), calculate half-wave thickness t = λ_center/(2×n) for central defect cavity layers (layers 11-12), then apply ±5% Gaussian perturbation to create initial population. Optimize all 22 individual layer thicknesses to maximize mean transmittance in passbands 4150-4350 nm and 4550-4750 nm while minimizing mean transmittance in stopbands 3600-4000 nm and 4850-5200 nm. Use coherent thin-film matrix method. Spectral evaluation range 3500-5300 nm. No metal layers. Maximum layer thickness 1000 nm, minimum 50 nm.",
